Design of Offline Assignment

fields:
User (name)
Listing (Id,Title,Description,Price,Username,Creatime,Category)
Category (name,count)

implemention

User hashtable Both Create or Check O(1) 

Listing hashtable [id]=item
1,CREATE_LISTING  O(1)
2,DELETE_LISTING  O(1)
3,GET_LISTING O(1)
 
Category hashtable [catname][listid]=>item
	 hashtable [catname]=>count
         highest_name //string
         highest_count //int
	 zset //sortedset

1,GET_CATEGORY O(logN)
If it is a read heavy operation, There are two optimized solutions:
1,we can used a sortedset or balance tree(red black tree) to maintain listing in order,so it doesnot need to sort every time,but it cost O(logN) to create_listing.
2,we can also used a hashtable to save it after first get,but it cost extra memory to store. 


2,GET_TOP_CATEGORY O(1)
if used sortedset , it cost O(logN) while create_listing & delete_listing to maintain sortedset.
if not sortedset , it cost O(N) while delete_listing of highest category to regenerate highest category //Usually delete of listing is a low frequency event, this is the preferred solution.


